CLOSURE_CHECKS_CLASSIFIER_AUDIT: {
  "schema_version": 1,
  "migration_run_id": "ccd7b51c-6e50-4e6d-ad9b-1bfbae5c705c",
  "snapshot_timestamp": "2026-05-21T04:22:03Z",
  "ticket_id": "7510-0198-3e2b-4ca5",
  "items": [
    {
      "original_text": "validate-issues.sh --quick --terse reports 0 orphan story/task warnings AND no non-closed story/task in the live tracker has parent_id=null, EXCLUDING tickets tagged standalone (intentional opt-out) and tickets tagged defer or dso-cleanup-pending (owned by 7271-e463). Before/after diff produced inside the sprint session by running validate-issues.sh --quick --terse immediately after orphan-cleanup.sh completes.",
      "original_section": "SC",
      "classification": {
        "label": "end-state",
        "ranking": 4,
        "rationale": "describes a durable system state where orphan story/task warnings are eliminated and validation passes, though the specification includes implementation details that blur the classification slightly"
      },
      "user_decision": "auto",
      "post_migration_section": "SC"
    },
    {
      "original_text": "ticket-create.sh emits \"ERROR: <type> ticket <id> created without --parent\" to stderr followed by \"To fix: ticket edit <id> --parent=<parent-id>\" whenever a non-bug, non-standalone-tagged ticket is created without --parent; exit code remains 0 (shell unit test).",
      "original_section": "SC",
      "classification": {
        "label": "end-state",
        "ranking": 4,
        "rationale": "describes a durable behavioral property of the ticket-creation system regarding error messaging and exit codes that persists after implementation"
      },
      "user_decision": "auto",
      "post_migration_section": "SC"
    },
    {
      "original_text": "ticket-link.sh retries up to 3 times with exponential backoff (configurable via ticket_link.retry_base_ms=250 and ticket_link.retry_max_ms=2000 with documented defaults), appends a structured JSON entry to the tracker link-failures log on persistent failure (fallback to ${REPO_ROOT}/.dso/link-failures.log when the tracker directory is absent), and emits structured ERROR to stderr (shell unit test).",
      "original_section": "SC",
      "classification": {
        "label": "end-state",
        "ranking": 4,
        "rationale": "describes durable behavioral properties of the system (retry logic, logging, error emission) that persist after implementation"
      },
      "user_decision": "auto",
      "post_migration_section": "SC"
    },
    {
      "original_text": "PRIMARY (load-bearing): A CI test under plugins/dso/tests/ scans every SKILL.md under plugins/dso/skills/ AND every agent dispatch prompt under plugins/dso/agents/ for ticket create story|task invocations and fails the build when any such invocation does not include an inline --parent= argument in the same command. All flagged sites are remediated within this epic's scope (not deferred). Three pre-existing missing-parent example sites are explicitly remediated: interface-contracts SKILL.md lines 82-87, tickets-health SKILL.md lines 113 and 116, preplanning/prompts/ui-designer-dispatch-protocol.md line 298.",
      "original_section": "SC",
      "classification": {
        "label": "end-state",
        "ranking": 4,
        "rationale": "describes a durable automated validation mechanism that continuously enforces a code requirement across the system"
      },
      "user_decision": "auto",
      "post_migration_section": "SC"
    },
    {
      "original_text": "BACKSTOP: Every orchestrator-context shell block calling ticket create story|task captures stderr via mktemp and runs ticket edit <id> --parent=<id> when \"created without --parent\" signal observed. Applied only at sites where literal-parent injection at the call site is unreliable (orchestrator constructs parent ID dynamically from session state); site list finalized in preplanning.",
      "original_section": "SC",
      "classification": {
        "label": "end-state",
        "ranking": 4,
        "rationale": "describes a durable system behavior where orchestrator-context shell blocks persistently capture stderr and conditionally run ticket edit, rather than a one-time migration task"
      },
      "user_decision": "auto",
      "post_migration_section": "SC"
    },
    {
      "original_text": "orphan-cleanup.sh runs the 5-step pipeline over all live orphans at execution time and exits 0 with a summary report counting each remediation type: (1) explicit-ID reparent using ticket reparent from 5efb-06ea, (2) bug retype via ticket edit --ticket_type, (3) test-fixture close, (4) duplicate-of-non-orphan close, (5) opus sub-agent batch-of-10 recommendation+execution. The script (a) acquires an exclusive flock on a tracker-side orphan-cleanup.lock to prevent concurrent invocations; (b) probes for the ticket reparent subcommand at startup and exits with a clear error if 5efb-06ea is not yet merged; (c) re-queries the live orphan list before each step rather than using the snapshot from step 1; (d) skips tickets tagged defer, dso-cleanup-pending, or standalone; (e) opus residuals (no confident parent) are tagged dso-cleanup-pending for handoff to 7271-e463 and reported under \"RESIDUAL\" in the summary rather than auto-closed.",
      "original_section": "SC",
      "classification": {
        "label": "transitional",
        "ranking": 4,
        "rationale": "describes a one-time migration script execution that remediates orphans and produces a completion report, not an ongoing system property"
      },
      "user_decision": "accept",
      "post_migration_section": "CC"
    },
    {
      "original_text": "**SC (self-use, Probe-1 remediation, architecture-vs-evidence audit 2026-05-16):** During the 7510 sprint, the new CI grep test (scanning `plugins/dso/skills/` and `plugins/dso/agents/` for ticket-create-without-`--parent`) is active and fires on at least one sprint PR (synthetic or organic). Verification (in-session, at sprint Phase I): `gh run list --workflow=ci.yml --branch=<sprint-branch> --json conclusion,jobs | jq '.[].jobs[] | select(.name | test(\"orphan|parent\"))'` shows the job ran; the three pre-existing missing-parent sites enumerated in the primary SC (interface-contracts:82-87, tickets-health:113/116, ui-designer-dispatch-protocol:298) are confirmed remediated by `grep -nE 'ticket create story|ticket create task' <those files> | grep -v -- '--parent='` returning 0 results.",
      "original_section": "SC",
      "classification": {
        "label": "transitional",
        "ranking": 4,
        "rationale": "describes verification of a one-time remediation task completed during a specific sprint, with concrete evidence collection as the completion criterion"
      },
      "user_decision": "accept",
      "post_migration_section": "CC"
    }
  ]
}
